        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">
          1. Off-Thread Audio Preprocessing with AudioWorklet
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          A common mistake in browser-based speech synthesis or recognition is running Fast Fourier Transforms (FFT) on the main UI thread, which causes noticeable stutter and dropped frames. In EdgeRuntimeHQ architectures, microphone audio is routed through an AudioWorkletProcessor:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li>Resampling from the native input sample rate (e.g., 44.1kHz or 48kHz) down to 16,000 Hz.</li>
          <li>Framing raw audio into 25ms windows with 10ms stride (400-sample window size with 160-sample hop).</li>
          <li>Applying Hann windowing and extracting 80 log-Mel filterbank channels.</li>
          <li>Transferring typed arrays to WebGPU storage buffers using zero-copy ArrayBuffer transfers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 2: Full Implementation Code -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">
          2. Complete In-Browser Whisper Implementation
